                    insight_suspended:      `The September intake again missed the floor on cohort or margin — the dean's office has moved to suspend or merge the MAS into a cheaper stackable format. The flagship ends as a distinct programme.`,

                    hint_cohort:            `Enrolment is below the ~60-student viable cohort — fixed costs aren't covered and margin can't reach the floor from here. Rebuild volume with relevance and a price the market bears before margin can recover.`,
                    hint_priceonly:         `You raised tuition hard to fix the ratio — the decision tree's trip-wire. The per-head number looks healthier, but elasticity is pricing the cohort away and total contribution, not the ratio, decides viability. Pull the raise back toward a price the market bears and rebuild the margin through design, not by pricing students out.`,
